---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ServiceHeading from "../components/ServiceHeading.astro";

const articles = [
  {
    n: "01",
    title: "The work",
    body: [
      `OCP3D solves old car problems with measured parts, engineering, and 3D printing. A surviving
       original goes on the bench; its critical dimensions go on the record; a new part earns its
       own status on a real vehicle. When an interface was never served in the first place, we
       engineer the useful adaptor instead of pretending it was an OEM part.`,
      `Pre-2000, unbranded, non-safety-critical parts only. Every measured dimension is published
       free. The parts cost money. The measurements never do.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    n: "02",
    title: "The old car problem",
    body: [
      `A discontinued clip is a problem. So is a wiper connection nobody ever designed, a cracked
       knob, an absent vent, or a small interface that turns an otherwise good car into a parked
       one. OCP3D treats the problem, not a nostalgia fantasy: identify the interface, document
       what is known, and build only what the evidence supports.`,
      `A 3D print is not a magic answer. It is a fast, physical way to test geometry, improve a
       measured design, and keep a machine in service while the industry has moved on.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    n: "03",
    title: "The first signal",
    body: [
      `File 01 was a sun visor clip for a 1983 Toyota Celica Supra. It was small, unavailable, and
       exactly the kind of failure that can sideline a car over a few grams of plastic. We measured
       it, printed it, revised it from physical evidence, and kept every result on the record.`,
      `Everything after it is the same promise: old car problem in, documented part path out.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    n: "04",
    title: "Keep the car. Not a profile of you.",
    body: [
      `Modern cars can log where you go and how you drive; that information can be sold, scored,
       and subscribed to. We do not need to argue with that system to know that a car without a
       modem remains an unusually private machine. Keeping it running is practical independence.`,
      `OCP3D follows the same rule: no trackers, no analytics, no ad pixels, and no third-party
       scripts. We retain only what a request or Dispatch signup genuinely needs, and say exactly
       what that is below.`,
    ],
  },
];

const retention = [
  ["TRACKERS", "0"],
  ["THIRD-PARTY SCRIPTS", "0"],
  ["ANALYTICS, AD PIXELS, SESSION RECORDING", "0"],
  ["FIELDS STORED ON DISPATCH SIGNUP", "1 — your email address"],
  ["WHAT IT IS USED FOR", "OCP3D Dispatch. Nothing else."],
  ["SOLD OR SHARED", "Never"],
  ["WAY OUT", "One click, on every issue"],
  ["DATA COLLECTED BY YOUR 1983 SUPRA SINCE 1983", "None"],
];
---
<Base title="Mission — OCP3D · Old Car Problems" sheet="MISSION · OCP3D">
  <section class="charter-page">
    <div class="wrap charter-wrap">
      <ServiceHeading
        eyebrow="OCP3D MISSION · ORBITAL SERVICE EST. 2026"
        title="Keep the old car in the future."
        lede="OCP3D exists to make the next useful part path visible: measured when possible, engineered when needed, and honest about every stage in between."
        file="MISSION · OCP3D"
        signal="PRESERVE · PROVE · PROGRESS"
      />

      <div class="mission-rule">
        <span class="rule-mark" aria-hidden="true">OCP3D</span>
        <p>Old cars are not a retreat from the future. They are machines worth carrying forward — with better evidence, more useful interfaces, and less surveillance attached.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="articles">
        {articles.map((a) => (
          <article class="article">
            <div class="art-no"><span class="eyebrow">TRANSMISSION</span><span class="numeral">{a.n}</span></div>
            <div class="art-body prose">
              <h2>{a.title}</h2>
              {a.body.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <section class="retention-panel">
        <div class="retention-head">
          <div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--amber">TRANSMISSION 04 — THE FACTS, STATED EXACTLY</p><h2>What we keep. What we do not.</h2></div>
          <p class="dense">Privacy is a working specification, not atmospheric copy. If the facts change, this record changes first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="retention">
          {retention.map(([k, v]) => (
            <><div><span class="eyebrow">{k}</span></div><div><span class="ret-v">{v}</span></div></>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="dense note">If measurement is ever needed, it will be first-party, aggregate, and stated here before it is switched on.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="mission-actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/registry/">Browse parts</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/request/">Log a problem</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .charter-page { background: linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground-deep) 25%, transparent), transparent 37%); }
  .charter-wrap { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .mission-rule { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr; gap: 22px; align-items: center; padding: 22px 26px; border: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground-deep) 80%, transparent); }
  .rule-mark { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 24px; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--signal); }
  .mission-rule p { max-width: 72ch; color: var(--body); }
  .articles { border: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule-2); }
  .article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr; gap: 30px; padding: 27px 30px; border-top: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule); background: var(--panel); }
  .article:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .article:nth-child(even) { background: var(--ground-deep); }
  .art-no { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; }
  .numeral { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 45px; line-height: 1; color: var(--signal); }
  .art-body { max-width: 700px; }
  .art-body h2, .retention-head h2 { font-size: 27px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .art-body p + p { margin-top: 14px; }
  .art-body p { color: var(--body); }
  .retention-panel { border: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule-2); background: var(--panel); }
  .retention-head { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 22px; padding: 25px 30px 18px; border-bottom: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule); }
  .retention-head .dense { max-width: 42ch; color: var(--steel); }
  .retention { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(240px, .7fr); background: var(--rule); gap: var(--bd-inner); }
  .retention > div { padding: 12px 16px; background: var(--ground-deep); }
  .ret-v { color: var(--paper); font-size: var(--t-dense); font-weight: 600; }
  .note { margin: 15px 30px 22px; color: var(--steel); max-width: 620px; }
  .mission-actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; padding: 10px 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .mission-rule, .article { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .mission-rule { gap: 8px; } .art-no { flex-direction: row; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; } .retention-head { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; } .retention { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .mission-rule, .article, .retention-head { padding: 20px; } .note { margin-inline: 20px; } }
</style>
